<header><p class="st-kicker">city state · Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><h1 class="st-title">Toniná</h1><p class="st-meta">500 CE – 909 CE (approx.) · capital Toniná</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A warlike Maya kingdom in the Ocosingo valley of Chiapas that captured a king of Palenque and recorded the last known Long Count date of the Classic era.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Toniná, anciently Popo', was built on a terraced hillside in the highlands of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chiapas">Chiapas</a>. A dynasty is attested from the 6th century, around 500 CE, and the city grew into a regional power at the western edge of the Maya lowlands.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Toniná's terraced acropolis rises some 70 metres above the valley and carried temples, palaces and ballcourts. Its sculptors favoured statues in the round and images of bound captives. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kinich-baaknal-chaak">K'inich B'aaknal Chaak</a> it waged war on <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/palenque">Palenque</a>, and in 711 Toniná captured Palenque's king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kan-joy-chitam-ii">K'an Joy Chitam II</a>, shown bound on a relief. A stucco frieze depicts the underworld with a skeletal figure holding a severed head.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Toniná outlasted most lowland kingdoms. A monument dated 909 bears the last known <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesoamerican-long-count-calendar">Long Count</a> date of the Classic Maya, after which royal rule ended. The site was later reoccupied on a small scale.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/tonina.jpg" alt="Toniná" width="320" height="215"><figcaption>Image: J. Antonio Cruz Coutiño · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Templo_Mayor_Tonin%C3%A1_1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>500 CE – 909 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>city state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>theocratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Toniná</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>K'inich B'aaknal Chaak</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Maya religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Classic Maya</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/mexico">Mexico</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Popo', Tonina</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=704&amp;focus=tonina" aria-label="Toniná on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2177 1550 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Toniná lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M2497 1806h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M2497 1806h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=704&amp;focus=tonina">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

